# One more WebChat initial-identity allowance (run-add-synthetic-customer.md step 0, branch "名额不足").
# 0050 never raises, resets or reopens a full allowance; more accounts come from a new browser application id with its own allowance.
# Copy to local-only/, fill the placeholders, chmod 0600; source it in the DATA_HOST configurator window. No secret in this file:
# the identity seal and the bootstrap DSN stay files ($RUN/identity-seal, $RUN/boot.dsn, run-34 §2.2).
TENANT_ID=<TENANT_ID>
# The two application ids registered in run-34 §2.2 (unchanged; used only to refuse a clash).
BROWSER_APPLICATION_ID=<WEBCHAT_APPLICATION_ID>
WORKBENCH_APPLICATION_ID=<WORKBENCH_APPLICATION_ID>
# The new id: never one already registered; [A-Za-z0-9][A-Za-z0-9._:-]{0,127}. initial_identity --create of the new accounts uses it.
ADDITIONAL_APPLICATION_ID=<WEBCHAT_APPLICATION_ID>-b
ADDITIONAL_ACCOUNTS=5
# Same label and signing key id as run-34 §2.2 (the allowance must match initial_identity's operator_label).
OPERATOR_LABEL=stage-owner
SIGNING_KEY_ID=<SIGNING_KEY_ID>
